    "4:07am": "Somewhere a nurse\nsigns her name\nfor the hundredth time.",
    "4:08am": "The dough has doubled\nunder its cloth.\nIt kept a secret all night.",
    "4:09am": "The alarm goes off.\nYou do the math.\nThe math is cruel.",
    "4:10am": "Ten past four.\nThe farmer's boots\nknow the way without him.",
    "4:11am": "Frost writes its name\non every windshield\nin the lot.",
    "4:12am": "The swimmer's bag\nis by the door.\nThe pool is still asleep.",
    "4:13am": "The monastery bell\ndoesn't ask\nif anyone is ready.",
    "4:14am": "The paperboy's bike\nclicks past.\nHeadlines land on wet grass.",
    "4:15am": "Quarter past four.\nThe moon leans on the hill\nlike it's tired too.",
    "4:16am": "The long-haul driver\nchanges the station.\nStill nothing but static.",
    "4:17am": "Steam from the cows.\nSteam from the bucket.\nSteam from the farmer's mouth.",
    "4:18am": "The airport wakes\nin fluorescent light.\nGate agents yawn in unison.",
    "4:19am": "The cat is awake.\nThe cat has been awake.\nThe cat has thoughts.",
    "4:20am": "Four twenty.\nThe dark is getting\nvery philosophical.",
    "4:21am": "Rowers on the river,\noars dipping\ninto black glass.",
    "4:22am": "Two twos.\nThe hour is\ntalking to itself.",
    "4:23am": "Your phone glows.\nNobody has texted.\nNobody is awake to.",
    "4:24am": "The streetlights hum\nthe only song\nthey know.",
    "4:25am": "A taxi idles.\nThe driver reads\nyesterday's news twice.",
    "4:26am": "The second bird\ndisagrees with the first.\nAnd so it begins.",
    "4:27am": "Dew settles on the mower\nleft out\nby someone braver.",
    "4:28am": "The tide turns\nwithout checking\nif anyone noticed.",
    "4:29am": "In the bakery window\nthe first loaves\nglow like small suns.",
    "4:30am": "Half past four.\nThe night is thinner now,\nlike old paper.",
    "4:31am": "A tanker's horn\nfar off in the bay.\nA long, low goodbye.",
    "4:32am": "Four thirty-two.\nThe digits climb\nlike a staircase.",
    "4:33am": "The radiator clanks.\nThe house is stretching\none pipe at a time.",
    "4:34am": "Someone is praying.\nSomeone is kneading.\nBoth need a little more time.",
    "4:35am": "The pool lights come on.\nBlue rectangles\nfloat up through the dark.",
    "4:36am": "The dog lifts one ear,\ndecides against it,\nand goes back down.",
    "4:37am": "The security guard\nfinishes his crossword.\nSeven down: dawn.",
    "4:38am": "The bread van pulls out.\nIts back doors\nbreathe steam.",
    "4:39am": "The sky in the east\nis not lighter.\nBut it's thinking about it.",
    "4:40am": "Twenty to five.\nThe orchard holds\nits breath in the frost.",
    "4:41am": "A jet climbs\nthrough the last stars,\nfull of sleeping strangers.",
    "4:42am": "The answer is 42.\nThe question is\nwhy am I awake.",
    "4:43am": "The window is a mirror\nwith you in it,\nholding a cup.",
    "4:44am": "Four forty-four.\nThree of a kind.\nThe night folds.",
    "4:45am": "Quarter to five.\nThe crows hold\ntheir first meeting.",
    "4:46am": "The bread comes out.\nThe whole street\nwill smell it soon.",
    "4:47am": "The night nurse\nchecks a chart\nby the light of the hall.",
    "4:48am": "The ferry crew\ncoils the ropes.\nThe river is still ink.",
    "4:49am": "A fox crosses the lot,\nlate for something\nonly foxes know.",
    "4:50am": "Ten to five.\nThe stars\nare closing their tabs.",
    "4:51am": "The monks are singing.\nThe hens are not.\nBoth will be soon.",
    "4:52am": "Coffee, first pot.\nThe kitchen light\nis the only sun.",
    "4:53am": "The trucker pulls in.\nThe diner sign flickers\nlike a wink.",
    "4:54am": "One window in the tower\nis lit.\nSomeone's deadline is today.",
    "4:55am": "Five to five.\nThe dark unbuttons\nits first button.",
    "4:56am": "The black sky\nhas gone the color\nof wet slate.",
    "4:57am": "The horizon is a rumor.\nThe birds\nhave heard it.",
    "4:58am": "Almost five.\nThe night sets down\nwhat it was carrying.",
    "4:59am": "Four takes off its coat\nand hangs it\non five's hook.",
    # 5am
    "5:00am": "Five o'clock.\nThe east tries on gray\nto see if it fits.",
    "5:01am": "One minute in\nand already a bird\nhas an opinion.",
    "5:02am": "Two minutes in.\nThe dark is thinner\nat the edges.",
    "5:03am": "A kettle ticks\nas it warms—\nthe house clearing its throat.",
    "5:04am": "Dew on the car.\nSomeone wrote WASH ME\nin the dark.",
    "5:05am": "Five oh five.\nTwo fives hold hands\naround a zero.",
    "5:06am": "The paper lands\nwith a slap.\nThe step forgives it.",
    "5:07am": "A runner passes,\nbreath in small clouds,\nchasing nobody.",
    "5:08am": "Blackbird first.\nThen robin.\nThen everyone at once.",
    "5:09am": "The moon lingers,\na thumbnail\nleft on the sky.",
    "5:10am": "Ten past five.\nThe fog is undecided\nabout the field.",
    "5:11am": "The cat takes the sill.\nThe sill\nwas always hers.",
    "5:12am": "Venus, low and bright,\nclocking out\nafter the night shift.",
