    "5:16am": "Spiderwebs on the fence,\nstrung with dew—\nthe night's receipts.",
    "5:17am": "The bakery light\nis the only one on.\nIt smells like a reason.",
    "5:18am": "Sprinklers hiss awake.\nThe lawn\ntakes its shower.",
    "5:19am": "Somewhere a rooster\nrehearses.\nHe's a little flat.",
    "5:20am": "Twenty past.\nThe grass is silver.\nThe cold is honest.",
    "5:21am": "A plane blinks east,\nfull of people\nwho haven't slept.",
    "5:22am": "Five twenty-two:\na pair of swans\non a pond of dark.",
    "5:23am": "The stop sign\nis red again.\nAll night it was just dark.",
    "5:24am": "First light on the roof.\nThe shingles\nremember their color.",
    "5:25am": "Five twenty-five.\nA two, tucked between fives,\nwide awake.",
    "5:26am": "The milkman is a myth.\nBut the porch light\nstill waits.",
    "5:27am": "The world is unopened mail.\nNo one\nhas read it yet.",
