    # 6am
    "6:00am": "Six o'clock.\nThe sun puts one foot\nover the hill.",
    "6:01am": "The alarm rings.\nThe hand that stops it\nis not yet yours.",
    "6:02am": "Snooze.\nNine more minutes\nof pretending.",
    "6:03am": "Light slips under the blind\nlike a note\npushed under a door.",
    "6:04am": "The kettle clears its throat.\nNo one else\nis up to hear it.",
    "6:05am": "Five past six.\nThe birds have been at it\nfor an hour already.",
    "6:06am": "Six oh six—\ntwo sixes, back to back,\nstill half asleep.",
    "6:07am": "The mailbox's shadow\nstretches west\nlike it wants to leave.",
    "6:08am": "The shower runs.\nBehind the curtain,\na person slowly forms.",
    "6:09am": "The radio says traffic.\nYou say nothing.\nThe toast agrees.",
    "6:10am": "Ten past six.\nThe cat is fed.\nThe cat disputes this.",
    "6:11am": "The first bus sighs\nat the empty stop\nand goes on anyway.",
    "6:12am": "The pillow still holds\nthe shape of a head\nthat left it.",
    "6:13am": "Dew on the car.\nA finger writes\nnothing in particular.",
    "6:14am": "Down the hall, a kid\nsleeps like a comma—\nnot finished yet.",
    "6:15am": "Quarter past six.\nThe sun is a quarter up.\nEven split.",
    "6:16am": "Six sixteen.\nSweet, says the clock,\nto no one.",
    "6:17am": "Coffee drips.\nEach drop a small yes\nto the day.",
    "6:18am": "Bare feet, cold floor.\nThe body files\nits first complaint.",
    "6:19am": "Steam on the mirror.\nYou wipe a hole\nand someone looks back.",
    "6:20am": "Twenty past six.\nA jogger passes,\nchasing her own breath.",
