    "6:22am": "Two twos after six.\nThe minute matches its socks.\nYou don't.",
    "6:23am": "The news reads a list\nof things that happened\nwhile you slept.",
    "6:24am": "Sun on the toaster.\nThe chrome shows\na sleepy face, stretched.",
    "6:25am": "Twenty-five past six.\nThe day is a cup\nnot yet spilled.",
    "6:26am": "Six twenty-six.\nThe digits nod\nat each other.",
    "6:27am": "Somewhere a snooze\nruns out of patience\nand starts to shout.",
    "6:28am": "Long shadows lie down\nacross the lawn\nand refuse to get up.",
    "6:29am": "The milk is low.\nThe note says milk.\nThe note is a week old.",
    "6:30am": "Half past six.\nThe hour folds\nneatly in the middle.",
    "6:31am": "A spoon rings the bowl.\nCereal rain.\nThe morning's first weather.",
    "6:32am": "Pink on the chimneys.\nThe roofs blush\nat being seen so early.",
    "6:33am": "Six thirty-three—\nthree threes for anyone\nwho's counting.",
    "6:34am": "The dog waits by the door\nwith the patience\nof a clock hand.",
    "6:35am": "Twenty-five to seven.\nThe sky files off\nits last star.",
    "6:36am": "Six thirty-six.\nSixes stacked like bowls\nin the drying rack.",
    "6:37am": "The blinds, opened,\nlet in a stripe\nof sun and dust.",
    "6:38am": "You put the wrong shoe\non the right foot\nand call it a start.",
