    "6:40am": "Twenty to seven.\nThe hallway light\nsurrenders to the window.",
    "6:41am": "A garbage truck\ntells the whole street\nwhat day it is.",
    "6:42am": "The kids stir.\nA blanket rises\nand sinks like a tide.",
    "6:43am": "The butter won't spread.\nThe toast gives way.\nSmall defeats, early.",
    "6:44am": "Six forty-four.\nDouble fours—\nthe day's first coincidence.",
    "6:45am": "Quarter to seven.\nThe sun shrugs off\nthe last of the hill.",
    "6:46am": "Six forty-six.\nSixes stand guard\naround the four.",
    "6:47am": "Keys, wallet, phone.\nThe morning liturgy,\nmuttered in the hall.",
    "6:48am": "The window shows the street\nand, faintly,\nyou in your robe.",
    "6:49am": "A neighbor's car coughs,\ncoughs again,\nand goes.",
    "6:50am": "Ten to seven.\nThe light stops arriving\nand starts staying.",
    "6:51am": "The radio hands off\nfrom weather to sports.\nYou hand off to socks.",
    "6:52am": "The last of the dark\nhides under the porch\nwith the spiders.",
    "6:53am": "A lunchbox closes\nwith the click\nof a small decision.",
    "6:54am": "The shadows pull in\nan inch, like sleeves\nbeing rolled.",
    "6:55am": "Five to seven.\nThe kettle's cooled.\nThe hour hasn't.",
