    "8:37am": "Traffic report:\neverywhere,\nas usual.",
    "8:38am": "Thirty-eight past.\nThe schoolyard empties\ninto quiet.",
    "8:39am": "The receptionist\nis already on\nher second hello.",
    "8:40am": "Twenty to nine.\nThe day starts asking\nwhat you'll do with it.",
    "8:41am": "The train stalls.\nA whole car practices\npatience together.",
    "8:42am": "A to-do list\nthat begins with\nwrite to-do list.",
    "8:43am": "The coffee line bends\naround a stranger\nreading a real book.",
    "8:44am": "The cat watches you leave\nlike it has plans\nof its own.",
    "8:45am": "Quarter to nine.\nThe last cool air\nclocks out.",
    "8:46am": "The commuter's nap\nends one stop\nafter it should.",
    "8:47am": "A bird on the wire\nsupervises\nthe whole intersection.",
    "8:48am": "Eight forty-eight.\nThree round bellies,\nbelted at the middle.",
    "8:49am": "Sunlight on the tracks.\nThe rails hum a note\nbefore the train.",
    "8:50am": "Ten to nine.\nThe day sharpens\nits pencil.",
    "8:51am": "Voicemail light blinking.\nSomeone called\nbefore you existed today.",
    "8:52am": "The printer warms up\nwith the sound\nof a small engine.",
